KG42.register("clusters-6036d2fcf2cdffbc95d9a94d",{"id":"27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v142-d-CL002","paper":"27-multiple_microgrid_trading","label":"Local quotation, request aggregation, and distributed price-adjustment clearing","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Local quotation, request aggregation, and distributed price-adjustment clearing","market_meaning":"Each microgrid calculates its local quotation and power purchase request at a fixed price; sellers aggregate neighbor requests, update prices according to the supply-demand gap, and continue iterative coordination. The global coupling equations provide a feasible clearing endpoint, and the Case 6 optimal price interpretation and the four-microgrid example retain their respective conditions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","pricing","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Local solving, request aggregation, and price adjustment are information dependencies within the same algorithm. The current iteration, next-round price, optimal price, and specific numerical example are retained separately; the supply-demand coupling equations constrain only feasible solutions and are not required to hold at every iteration. The price function and the price coordination function are not merged into one node merely because they use the same numerical values.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Quotation, request aggregation, and price updating together form an identifiable distributed coordination loop. The global configuration chain serves as endpoint constraint support, and the power purchase chain serves as the input-output interface; cost configuration, product, participation permission, and accounting obligations each retain independent primary attribution.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the calculation responsibility, price inputs, and non-negativity of the local electricity sales quotation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Carries price exchange and neighbor request aggregation, connecting local quotation and price adjustment activities."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the supply-demand-gap-driven price update and local execution responsibility."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Retains the price meaning of price adjustment and the conditional optimal price relation; repeated update expressions are not counted as an additional rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References the power purchase calculation and disclosure interface, whose branch decision is primarily attributed to CL001."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"References the global feasible coupling and configuration objective, explaining the clearing endpoint of the price-adjustment residual."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x_E_ji","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C010"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g21-e021","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"The request sent by the buyer is received by the corresponding seller; when switching to the receiving seller's perspective, indices must be relabeled, and unrelabeled coordinates in the opposite direction cannot be directly equated."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x03","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"The row vector formed by the seller from neighbor requests enters the same-round price update; this request vector must be distinguished from the local scalar electricity sales quotation."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-eps-s","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x02","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g16-e016","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"The local electricity-sale offer obtained with the current price fixed serves as the supply input in the price-adjustment difference of that round."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g19-e019","v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g24-e024"],"rationale":"The two chains separately state the same update and its direction interpretation from the perspectives of coordination responsibility and price function; the original binding is retained, and the update formula serves only once as a display of scientific expression."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g15-e015","v141-b-g19-e019","v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g24-e024"],"rationale":"The price update uses the supply-demand residual of the global coupling constraint. The equality at a feasible endpoint and the residual of intermediate iterations are explained separately; no new C edge is added merely by narrative order."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x01","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_i","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g23-e023"],"rationale":"The updated price participates as a fixed input in the electricity-purchase calculation in the next round; the connection expresses the inter-iteration interface and does not force this round's input to equal the next round's output."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"All reference the same electricity-purchase request function, and all original chains and edges remain accessible."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g15-e015","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"All are the electricity-sale offer function of the same mechanism; unified node display does not eliminate differences in quantity roles."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g21-e021","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"The coordinators are all the microgrids themselves; no external centralized operator is introduced on this basis."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g19-e019","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"All reference the same distributed price-signal coordination function."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM05","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::pricing.inter_area","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.inter_area","v141-c-R010::V::pricing.inter_area"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R010::V::pricing.inter_area","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g38-e038"],"rationale":"All are inter-microgrid pricing functions; they are not merged with coordination.price_signal."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM06","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::clearing.inter_area","v141-c-R010::V::clearing.inter_area"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::clearing.inter_area","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g24-e024"],"rationale":"The two chains reference the same clearing function, but configuration feasibility and price-adjustment implementation are still retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_i","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x01","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g23-e023"],"rationale":"The sale prices at the same i, k serve respectively as a local fixed input and as a signal to be updated; the local roles of theta and x are retained, and it is not equivalent to the optimal price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-lambda","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"All are the complete price vector exchanged in the same round and fixed in local computation, and are not merged with a single price component."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-eps-s","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-eps","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x02","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g15-e015","v141-b-g16-e016","v141-b-g18-e018","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"They correspond to the same electricity-sale offer coordinate in the decomposition model and its local iterative value; global variables, local offers, and price-adjustment inputs are retained separately, and intermediate values do not automatically satisfy the global coupling."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM10","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-E-s","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x002","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x03","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g06-e006","v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"Each record uses the coordinate form of the same seller row vector, but the tense interpretation of neighbor requests, sales vectors, and offered-energy wording has not yet been unified; they are tentatively treated as candidate alternative expressions of the same type of object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM11","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-p01","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"All are positive step-size factors of the same update step; the original parameter record and the unspecified step-size sequence are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM12","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-A","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-A","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-p02","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g06-e006"],"rationale":"The directed adjacency matrix is explicitly shared by the same mechanism, and the roles of selection, configuration, and price adjustment in each chain are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM13","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-e-i","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-ei","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-p03","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g10-e010","v141-b-g20-e020"],"rationale":"All are unit column selectors for the same index i under the same system dimension, and the bindings in different expressions are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM14","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g19-e019","v141-b-g22-e022"],"rationale":"The three occurrences are the same iterative update formula, respectively highlighting supply input, execution responsibility, and price result; only a formula display representative is selected, and the different functional bindings are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM15","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g24-e024"],"rationale":"All are the same explanation of price direction under excess demand and are not counted as independent price-adjustment rules."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G01","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R002 only declares solving local subproblems and the non-negativity of offers; the current C catalogue does not fully carry local objective (7) and the electricity-sale and generation solutions of each case. The global balance equation cannot replace each round's local optimization.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g16-e016","v141-b-g17-e017","v141-b-g18-e018","v141-b-g25-e025","v141-b-g30-e030","v141-b-g33-e033","v141-b-g34-e034","v141-b-g35-e035"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C is to supplement, within the original scope, citable objects for the local objective and supply branches and to verify branch feasibility; D does not add formulas or rewrite frozen chains."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"It only declares that the step size is positive; this cannot guarantee convergence for an arbitrary step-size sequence. Algorithm 1 also does not give an executable stopping threshold.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-p01","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supplement source-supported applicability conditions for the step size and stopping criteria; until then, retain only the iterative mechanism and do not claim that any implementation reaches optimal clearing."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G03","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R004 explicitly interprets the sales row vector as pooled neighbor requests, R010 calls it an offered-energy vector, and R005 further binds it to supply nodes. The same coordinate form cannot yet eliminate the temporal differences among requests, offers, and feasible transactions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-E-s","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x002","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x03","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g06-e006","v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify and have upstream clarify the temporal status and local roles of each record; maintain the independent identity of the candidate alternative mapping and the scalar offer."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G04","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The privacy limitation is supported by statements on communication scope and confidentiality of local information, but node proposal v141-b-g03-p01 has still not been approved; this cluster cannot treat that proposal as an existing graph node.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C010","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g21-e021","v141-b-g03-e15"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-p01"],"required_work":"A human is to decide the ontological handling of the proposal and subsequent C expression; currently only the existing disclosure constraints are retained, and no new node is inserted."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G05","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R010 simultaneously contains the iterative price, the Case 6 optimality relation, and the four-microgrid Case 4 example. Their conditions differ; the example's marginal-cost relation or optimal value cannot be unconditionally imposed on each round's signal.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X004","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e023","v141-b-g03-e01","v141-b-g03-e02","v141-b-g03-e06"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check item by item the optimality, case, and example qualifications; retain the conditional juxtaposition and do not establish an identity mapping between iterative values and optimal values or between general costs and the example's common cost."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G06","category":"unverified_source","description":"The algorithm, economic interpretation, and object correspondences all use unaudited evidence permitted by the experiment and have not undergone B audit or C2 independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g19-e019","v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g21-e021","v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g24-e024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the algorithm transcription, indices, update direction, and all mappings; maintain B's unverified status."}]},"rule_refs":["27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R002","27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R004","27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R005","27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R010","27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R001","27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-29a9bef8bb03bc72","COMP-cb8f993b6ad4c7bc","KG40-64e89df75d6f5be0","KG40-7b5176e5e40aa7c7","KG40-a9ae52fd85070f81","KG40-ae777dabd8002658"]});
